  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of size NNN – [A1,A2,…,AN][A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_N][A1​,A2​,…,AN​].\n\nThere will be B1+B2+…+BNB_1 + B_2 + \\ldots + B_NB1​+B2​+…+BN​ total events, with exactly BiB_iBi​ events of type iii. The type iii events will happen before the type i+1i + 1i+1 events for each 1≤i&lt;N1 \\le i \\lt N1≤i&lt;N.\n\nIn an event of type XXX, you must do **exactly one** of the following:\n\n\nAdd 111 to AXA_XAX​, or\nAdd 222 to AYA_YAY​ for any Y≠XY \\ne XY=X.\nNote that the choice is made independently for each event: in particular, you can make different choices even for different events of the same type.\n\nAfter all the events are done, you want to minimize max⁡(A1,A2,…,AN)\\max(A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_N)max(A1​,A2​,…,AN​). Find this minima value.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of three lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN - the size of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nThe third line contains NNN integers - B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum value of max⁡(A1,A2,…,AN)\\max(A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_N)max(A1​,A2​,…,AN​) after all events.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai,Bi≤1091 \\le A_i, B_i \\le 10^91≤Ai​,Bi​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "6\n2\n3 5\n1 2\n3\n1 2 1\n2 1 1\n3\n27 72 99\n38 54 66\n2\n1000000000 1000000000\n1000000000 1000000000\n4\n2 2 5 4\n3 3 1 3\n2\n10 20\n1 1",
        "output": "6\n3\n131\n2000000000\n7\n20",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 1 : There are 333 total events, 111 of type 111 and 222 of type 222. Here is what an optimal procedure looks like:\n\nEvent 111 of type 111 : We choose the first option to add to X=1X = 1X=1 itself. The array is updated to [4,5][4, 5][4,5].\nEvent 222 of type 222 : We choose the first option to add to X=2X = 2X=2 itself. The array is updated to [4,6][4, 6][4,6].\nEvent 333 of type 222 : We choose the second option to add to some other YYY, and we choose Y=1Y = 1Y=1. The array is updated to [6,6][6, 6][6,6].\n\nWe achieved a maxima of 666 which is the smallest we can do."
      }
    ]
  },
